            ],
            "body": [
                "The smallest version of this scenario can be played on a 4'×4' table with 2 players. The chart below indicates how big your table should be for the number of players you have. If you have more than eight players, don’t hesitate to get creative with table placement.\n<B># of Players <indent=200> Table Size</indent><indent=400># of Objectives</indent></B>\n2 players <indent=240> 4’×4’</indent> <indent=400> 4x50 mm Objectives</indent>\n4 players <indent=240> 4’×6’</indent> <indent=400> 5x50 mm Objectives</indent>\n6 players <indent=240> 4’×8’</indent> <indent=400> 6x50 mm Objectives </indent>\n8 players <indent=240> 4’×8’</indent> <indent=400> 7x50 mm Objectives </indent>\nNext, terrain. The Legendary Event uses terrain that evokes a sense of fighting over a volcanic caldera. In the WARMACHINE app, you will find rules for the Volcanic Vent terrain we used—feel free to substitute a forest for this terrain if you do not have something appropriate available. Make sure to use roughly even amounts of volcanic vents, hills, and obstructions when selecting terrain.",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "colorHex": "",
            "textColorHex": "",
            "mediaPath": "",
            "widthPerc": 100,
            "mediaWidth": 0,
            "mediaHeight": 0,
            "caption": [
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "isSub": false,
            "helpTermSorting": [],
            "helpTermIds": []
        },
        {
            "guidStr": "dd793372-ecc1-47da-a97f-98fa0c6c8802",
            "name": [
                "Name",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "isLive": false,
            "metadata": "",
            "deleted": false,
            "type": "Body",
            "topMarginOverride": -1,
            "bottomMarginOverride": -1,
            "leftMarginOverride": -1,
            "rightMarginOverride": -1,
            "title": [
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
            ],
            "body": [
                "We recommend 10 pieces of terrain for a 4'×4' table, 14 for a 4'×6' table, and 18 for a 4'×8' table. When picking terrain, make sure you have several 3\" templates. As described below in the \"Running the Dragon\" section, you will have multiple opportunities to add these during play.\nAdditionally, you will need several 50 mm objectives, one of which will be used as the Lash of Horva itself while the others will serve as Soul Pyres.",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                "",
                ""
